## DESCRIPTION
## Find the solution of a linear system based on its reduced row echelon form. 
## This problem has no solution. 
## ENDDESCRIPTION

## KEYWORDS('reduced row echelon form', 'solution')

## DBsubject('Linear algebra')
## DBchapter('Homogeneous and Nonhomogeneous Solutions')
## DBsection('Problem')
## Date('September 5, 2011')
## Author('Peter Staab')
## Institution('Fitchburg State University')

# updated 2023.11.10

DOCUMENT();    # This should be the first executable line in the problem.
loadMacros('PGstandard.pl', 'PGML.pl', 'parserRadioMultiAnswer.pl','PGcourse.pl');

Context("Vector")->variables->are(t => 'Real', s => 'Real');

# Define all variables used in the problem statement and solution

$a13 = random(-4, 4);
$a14 = random(-4, 4);
$b1  = random(-4, 4);
$a23 = random(-4, 4);
$a24 = random(-4, 4);
$b2  = random(-4, 4);
$b3  = non_zero_random(-4, 4);

# Now begin with the Problem Statement

$rma = RadioMultiAnswer([
    ['There is no solution.'],
    ['The solution is %s', Compute('0')]
    ],    0);

BEGIN_PGML

Consider the following matrix in reduced row echelon form: 

[```
\left[
\begin{array}{rrrr|r}
1 & 0 & [$a13] & [$a14]  & [$b1] \\
0 & 1 & [$a23] & [$a24] & [$b2]\\
0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & [$b3] \\
\end{array}
\right] ```]

[_]{$rma}

Write the solution to the associated linear system in vector form using [` s`] or [`t`] as free variables if necessary.  For example use [|<1,2,3>+t<4,5,6>|]* or 
[|<1,2,3>+t<4,5,6>+s<7,8,9>|]*.

END_PGML

BEGIN_PGML_SOLUTION
The last row in the matrix corresponds to the equation [` 0 = [$b3]`] which is false, so there is no solution. 
END_PGML_SOLUTION

ENDDOCUMENT();
